_0 = L$.","caption":["The plane through the tip of the soliton ($x = 0$, $r_0 = L$), $\\phi = 0$ on the right and $\\phi = \\pi$ on the left, conformal to a whole strip with the tip $\\rho = 0$ down its middle. The two edges are the conformal boundary at opposite sides of the circle $\\tau$, each at an infinite proper distance $\\rho$.","Light crosses from one edge to the other through the tip in $ct = 2.80\\,L^2/r_0$. A free particle released from rest falls toward the tip, where clocks at rest run slowest, passes through it, and swings back and forth across it; the two drawn are released at $\\rho = L/2$ and $\\rho = L$, and the one released farther out takes longer over each swing."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[-1.5708,-0.9425],[1.5708,-0.9425],[1.5708,4.0841],[-1.5708,4.0841]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[-1.5708,-0.9425],[1.5708,-0.9425],[1.5708,4.0841],[-1.5708,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"boundary","points":[[1.5708,-0.9425],[1.5708,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"boundary","points":[[-1.5708,-0.9425],[-1.5708,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"centre","points":[[0.0,-0.9425],[0.0,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.5286,-0.9425],[0.5286,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[-0.5286,-0.9425],[-0.5286,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.9219,-0.9425],[0.9219,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[-0.9219,-0.9425],[-0.9219,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[1.3302,-0.9425],[1.3302,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[-1.3302,-0.9425],[-1.3302,4.0841]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,-0.7854],[1.5708,-0.7854]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,0.0],[1.5708,0.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,0.7854],[1.5708,0.7854]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,1.5708],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,2.3562],[1.5708,2.3562]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t","points":[[-1.5708,